WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:07.080
Hey David, you talk a lot about believing
women, but what would you do if you were falsely

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.940
accused of sexual assault?

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.230
Let's discuss it.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:14.620
This actually came up when I was on, remember
that show I went on in LA, the Jesse Lee Peterson

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:15.620
show.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.570
We were talking about the Brett Kavanaugh
hearings and he asked me in some way, would

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:22.689
you want to be accused of a sexual assault
you didn't commit?

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.439
And I said, that's not really a question,
Jesse.

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:28.380
No one, I don't, I don't want anyone accused
of a crime that they didn't commit.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.380
Of course.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:34.180
Uh, and in fact, there was a movement to do
this at a time when I was covering the Kavanaugh

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.180
hearings.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:39.750
I started hearing from people who said, David,
we're going to go to your local papers.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.980
We're going to claim that you sexually assaulted
someone.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:47.010
And my understanding is that some of those
allegations were actually made and they went

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.410
nowhere because they obviously were not credible.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.290
But let's answer the question as asked.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:56.140
False rape or sexual assault allegations are
very rare.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.730
But when they happen, they should be punished.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:01.580
And I've said that for a very long time, but
let's play it out.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:05.420
What would I do if I were accused of sexual
assault or rape?

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:07.630
And I had not done anything wrong.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:11.000
First and foremost, I would say nothing and
I would immediately call a lawyer.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.170
Now I know that that already puts me in a
position of privilege, right?

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:16.860
Not everybody can afford a lawyer.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:22.700
Um, well if the police want to talk to you,
uh, if you are being compelled to talk to

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:24.890
them, then you can request a lawyer.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:29.090
And if you are not being compelled to talk
to them, then I simply would not talk to them.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:30.910
But I would immediately reach out to a lawyer.

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:33.620
I would not attempt to contact the accuser.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:36.490
I would not attempt to contact the accuser's
family.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:42.600
I would immediately think to myself, who might
be able to either provide an alibi or be a

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.580
witness in some way.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.520
I would immediately try to put in writing
whatever interactions I may have had in my

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:55.270
life with the accuser, if there are any, if
it's genuinely someone I don't even know,

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:58.960
I would of course not have any interactions
to write down.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:03.360
But if there's someone that is known to me,
I would immediately put in writing interactions.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.150
I would check social media records.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:09.119
I would check email, whatever and and really
categorize for myself what the interactions

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:10.399
have been if any.

00:02:10.399 --> 00:02:11.700
Now I get it.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.340
False allegations.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:20.000
Anytime that you have a system that allows
people to um, uh, make a complaint that they

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.990
have been victimized by, by someone else,
there will be some percentage of either straight

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:31.630
up false allegations or mistaken identity
problems were an accuser believes it was this

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.640
person when in reality it was that person.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:39.110
What I, I really want to state here is I'm
glad to answer the question about what I would

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:40.110
do.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:41.680
These are not common situations.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.150
I don't want to give them more importance
than they deserve.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:53.120
I believe it is a far bigger problem for those
who are victimized by sexual assault or rape

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.930
to never have justice done to the perpetrator.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:02.540
That is a far bigger problem mathematically
than false rape allegations.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:07.459
Most importantly, the most important thing
that I do in order to avoid allegations of

00:03:07.459 --> 00:03:14.400
any kind is I don't sexually harass or assault
people, which in 99.99, whatever percent of

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.950
the cases is actually your best insurance.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:23.050
If I'm missing something, if the actions I
would take are not the right ones, let me

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.750
know what I'm missing.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.500
We have a great bonus show coming up for you
today.

